model g14_edges
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "T, tally 2.1.6 (#89, P7; #48, P8), G14: L §7.6's limits load sees, each at its edge, where it loads and answers (one past each is codes/m0's basic/limit-* and basic/s1-*, LOAD-LIMIT): an index of 1 000 000 keys and a literal range an ask steps through of as many; a day range by 10 whose last period ends on 9999-12-31, the end of time, as a whole period; a range index's end and step of 18 digits; a key offset and its pos(k) guard of 18 digits (the guard never holds, so the base rule answers); unit powers of 64, PLN and %, written and reached by * (PLN^32 * PLN^32)."

source plan "T's invented plan"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

index ns = 1..1000000

index ds = day 9999-12-02..9999-12-31 by 10

index big = 1..999999999999999999 by 999999999999999999

index ks = 1..3

input base: int

input y: num PLN^64

input h: num PLN^32

input p: num %^64

def x[k in ks]: int at reader
  rule base = base
  rule back beats base = x[k - 999999999999999999] + base when pos(k) > 999999999999999999

def sq: num PLN^64 = h * h

version plan_2026
  cite plan
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  base = 1
  y = 2 PLN^64
  h = 3 PLN^32
  p = 1 %^64

ask keys: max(pos(k) for k in ns), max(pos(k) for k in big), max(k for k in 1..1000000)

ask last_period: max(pos(k) for k in ds), max(start_of(k) for k in ds), max(end_of(k) - 1 day for k in ds)

ask offset: x[3] law 2026-06-30

ask powers: y, sq, p
